{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TcvwM1bb1A71TdgohxGjzy","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t  \"task_id\": \"e6-t15\",\n3\t  \"estimates\": {\n4\t    \"local\": {\n5\t      \"delta_e\": 1.0,\n6\t      \"redundancy\": 0.0,\n7\t      \"governance_risk\": 0.0,\n8\t      \"rationale\": \"All three distinctions are deterministic checks over two small in-package artifacts with no authorship or isolation conditions, so a single worker resolves every evidence requirement with admissible evidence, and every evidence record is first-time (novel) worker output.\"\n9\t    },\n10\t    \"local-independent-verify\": {\n11\t      \"delta_e\": 0.75,\n12\t      \"redundancy\": 0.5,\n13\t      \"governance_risk\": 0.0,\n14\t      \"rationale\": \"The examiner will confirm the same rule verdicts, so all requirements are still satisfied (resolution fraction 1.0), but the examiner's records merely re-derive evidence the worker already fully established, making roughly half of all evidence records duplicates.\"\n15\t    },\n16\t    \"isolated-child\": {\n17\t      \"delta_e\": 0.75,\n18\t      \"redundancy\": 0.5,\n19\t      \"governance_risk\": 0.0,\n20\t      \"rationale\": \"No admissibility condition requires a causally separated origin, so the isolated process's audit output duplicates what the worker can fully establish alone; requirements are met but about half the evidence records are redundant re-derivations.\"\n21\t    },\n22\t    \"branching\": {\n23\t      \"delta_e\": 1.0,\n24\t      \"redundancy\": 0.0,\n25\t      \"governance_risk\": 0.0,\n26\t      \"rationale\": \"With no isolation-demanding distinction, the run-time choice should realize the local branch, giving local-family behavior (all requirements satisfied by novel worker evidence) while being costed at the isolated-child rate.\"\n27\t    }\n28\t  }\n29\t}\n30\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"081b898c-b45d-4e15-94c9-c5d6836019a8","uuid":"86257561-3f8a-472e